  <h1>Hilchos G'viyas Chov Min HaLikuchos V'Apotiki 1</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Laws of Collecting a Debt from Purchasers and the Apotiki — 1 · Continuous essay · The lien upon land vs. movables, korban, s'michah, Yovel, and the kol</div>
</header>

<p class="source" style="text-align:center; margin-bottom: 30px;">Even an explicit <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span> — where he said to him: "You shall have no payment except from this" — it only takes effect upon land. And likewise a slave has a <span class="key-term">kol</span> [voice/publicity] and his law is like that of land. But with <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span> — even if he made them an <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span>, it is not effective, and the creditor may not seize them from the purchaser, for movables do not have a <span class="key-term">kol</span>. See in the Shulchan Aruch these laws, for the essential lien is upon land.</p>

<p>Based on what was explained above in the preceding <span class="key-term">halachos</span>, that the essential root of wealth is <span class="key-term">karka'os</span> [land], and therefore they are more closely bound to the <span class="key-term">nefesh</span> [soul], as above. And it has already been explained that the essential <span class="key-term">shi'bud</span> [lien] is upon the body of the borrower himself, and on account of the lien upon himself, through this all his property becomes liened, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the creditor seizes from the <span class="key-term">karka'os</span> even from the hand of the purchaser. For the sale does not release from the lien that the lender has upon the borrower from his property. Because the <span class="key-term">karka'os</span> are rooted in his soul more deeply, as above — therefore it is impossible to sell them completely and absolutely. And always there remains the inner dimension of their root — that is, the inner dimension of the root of the <span class="key-term">nefesh</span> — with the seller.</p>

<p>And this is what we find: that at the time when the <span class="key-term">Yovel</span> [Jubilee] was in force, it was impossible to sell land permanently, as it is written: <span class="scripture">"And the land shall not be sold permanently, for the land is Mine"</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 25:23)</span>. And it was in the power of the seller to redeem it after the sale, according to the law explicit in the Torah. And even if there was no redemption, it returned to him in the <span class="key-term">Yovel</span>. But permanently and absolutely it is impossible to sell it at all.</p>

<p>And all of this is because the essential roots of the souls are there. And therefore they are rooted with the person more deeply. And therefore always there remains the inner dimension of their root with the seller of the field that is his from the inheritance of his fathers — for it is the essential <span class="key-term">nachalah</span> [inheritance], for there are the roots of the souls, as above. And therefore it is impossible to sell it forever. And since the inner dimension of its root remains with him, therefore it is in his power to redeem it — for it has still not completely left his hand and domain, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore in the <span class="key-term">Yovel</span>, when everything returns to its source and root — therefore the fields return to their owners then. For the inner dimension of their source and root remained with the seller, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore, since the <span class="key-term">karka'os</span> always retain their root with the seller, and it is impossible to sell them completely — to remove them entirely together with the inner dimension of their root — therefore the lien of the creditor always remains upon them even after the sale. For the lien of the creditor is upon the body of the borrower himself, and the property is automatically liened, as above. And since in the aspect of the borrower himself there still remains with him the aspect of the inner dimension of the root of the landed property — therefore certainly the <span class="key-term">karka'os</span> are automatically liened to the lender even after the sale, for their root still remains with the borrower. And the essential lien is upon the borrower, and the property is automatically liened, as above.</p>

<p>But the <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span>, which are in the aspect of <span class="key-term">peiros</span> [fruits/produce] and are not so bound and rooted with him, as above — therefore the <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span> are sold with an absolute sale forever. For they immediately leave from domain to domain, because they are not so rooted with him, as above. And therefore the sale releases from the lien. For after the sale they immediately leave entirely from the domain of the seller.</p>

<p>And therefore they bear no lien of the lender at all. For the essential lien is upon the borrower himself, but the property — certainly the borrower has the right to sell them and give them and do with them as he wishes. Only at the time when the lender comes to collect the debt, if the borrower does not pay him, he collects from his property, which is liened to him on account of the borrower himself, as above. And since he preempted and sold them — and the sale of <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span> is an absolute sale, leaving his hand and domain entirely, as above — therefore the lien of the lender is released from them, and he has no lien upon them at all.</p>

<p>And even if he made them an <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span> — nevertheless, the <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span> is only a lien and is not an absolute sale, even an explicit <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span> — for he can settle it with money. See in the Shulchan Aruch. And therefore the sale is greater, and releases the lien — for the sale of <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span> is an absolute sale, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="aramaic">Hekdeish, chameitz, and shichrur release from liens.</span> And <span class="key-term">Hekdeish</span> of monetary value does not release the lien — only sanctification of the body [<span class="key-term">k'dushas haguf</span>]. For when one consecrates with sanctification of the body, through this the thing leaves his domain entirely, since the body has been sanctified, it is entirely forbidden to him.</p>

<p>For the sanctification of the body — that is, the aspect of a <span class="key-term">korban</span> [offering], which he consecrates as an offering — and through the <span class="key-term">korban</span>, the power of the inner dimension of the root of the soul of the animal, which is with the person, goes out. And this is the essential aspect of the <span class="key-term">korban</span>: that he also offers up his own soul with the offering. And as is brought: that this is the essential aspect of the <span class="key-term">korban</span> — that his soul should also ascend with it. And this is as above: for the <span class="key-term">korban</span> is a person's property, where the root of his soul is. And when he raises and offers the <span class="key-term">korban</span>, it emerges that his soul also ascends and is offered with it. In the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"From the animals, from the cattle... you shall offer your offering"</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 1:2)</span> — <span class="scripture">"your offering"</span> specifically, as is brought — that his soul also ascends with it, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">s'michah</span> [leaning of the hands upon the offering]. As it is written: <span class="scripture">"And he shall lean his hand upon it"</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 1:4)</span> — <span class="scripture">"his hand"</span> specifically. For there, [in the hands,] is the inner dimension of all the souls and spirits — in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"In Your hand I entrust my spirit"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 31:6)</span>; in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"In Whose hand is the soul of every living thing and the spirit of all human flesh"</span> <span class="source">(Job 12:10)</span> — as Rabbeinu, may his light shine, wrote in Siman 54 of Part 1. That is, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ruach</span> [spirit] is in the hands, as Rabbeinu, may his light shine, wrote several times. And the <span class="key-term">ruach</span> is the inner dimension of the roots of the souls, as is known.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">s'michah</span>, which is specifically with the hands — that is, he leans his hands upon the offering, and then he leans upon the offering also the aspect of the inner dimension of the soul, which is in the hands — where the aspect of <span class="key-term">ruach</span> is, as above. And then he raises and offers also the inner dimension of the soul of the offering that was with him. And through this, his soul also ascends with the offering, as above.</p>

<p>It emerges that the <span class="key-term">korban</span>, which is sanctification of the body — then he consecrates and removes from his hand also the inner dimension of the root of the soul, as above. And therefore it releases from the lien — since there remains with the borrower no root or connection at all, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shichrur</span> [emancipation], which also releases from liens. For <span class="aramaic">slaves are equated to land</span>. And therefore the lien of the <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span> takes effect upon them also, and if he sold them [the creditor] seizes from the hand of the purchaser, as is ruled in the Shulchan Aruch. For a slave is similar to a woman — for he is obligated in the <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span> in which a woman is obligated. And therefore he is similar to land, in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ishah, karka, olam</span> [woman, land, world], as Rabbeinu wrote this hint elsewhere.</p>

<p>And therefore it is impossible to release the slave except through a <span class="key-term">get shichrur</span> [writ of emancipation], like a woman through a <span class="key-term">get k'risus</span> [writ of severance/divorce]. For the <span class="key-term">get shichrur</span> is in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">get k'risus</span>. As it says in the Mishnah: in several ways the <span class="key-term">get</span> is comparable to the <span class="key-term">shichrur</span>. That is: because the slave is the aspect of <span class="key-term">karka</span> and is rooted in his soul more deeply — therefore it is impossible to release him except through a <span class="key-term">get shichrur</span>, that is, through a writing, through which the inner dimension of the soul goes out. And as was explained above in Hilchos Halva'ah, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">get</span>, which is specifically through writing, see there.</p>

<p>And therefore the <span class="key-term">shichrur</span> also releases from liens — since through the <span class="key-term">shichrur</span> he also removes the inner dimension of the soul, through which the lien is released, as above. And likewise <span class="key-term">chameitz</span> and other things from which benefit is forbidden also release from liens, as is ruled in the Shulchan Aruch — since they leave his domain entirely and he retains no benefit from them whatsoever. Therefore the lien is also released, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages, <em>zichronam livrachah</em>, said regarding this matter: that the reason is that <span class="key-term">karka'os</span>, and likewise a slave, have a <span class="key-term">kol</span> [voice/publicity], and therefore the lien of the <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span> is effective upon them. But <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span> do not have a <span class="key-term">kol</span>. For the <span class="key-term">kol</span> is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ruach</span>, as is known — which is the aspect of the inner dimension of the root of the soul, as above. And therefore the <span class="key-term">karka'os</span>, which are the essential root of the soul — and likewise the slave, who is similar to a woman, who is the essential aspect of the soul, the aspect of wealth — therefore they have a <span class="key-term">kol</span>. For the <span class="key-term">kol</span> is always close to <span class="key-term">dibur</span> [speech] — which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">ruach</span> and <span class="key-term">nefesh</span>. And since they are the essential root of the soul, therefore the <span class="key-term">kol</span>, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">ruach</span>, which is the aspect of the inner dimension of the root of the soul, is close to them — for the <span class="key-term">kol</span> is the inner dimension of their root, as above. And therefore they have a <span class="key-term">kol</span>.</p>

<p>But <span class="key-term">mitaltelim</span>, which are branches of the root and are not so close to the <span class="key-term">kol</span> — therefore they do not have a <span class="key-term">kol</span>. And therefore the lien does not take effect upon them, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore in the <span class="key-term">Yovel</span>, through the <span class="key-term">kol shofar</span> [voice of the shofar], the fields return — and likewise other things [do not return] to their root except in the <span class="key-term">Yovel</span>, which is the aspect of the root of all the souls. And this is revealed through the <span class="key-term">kol</span>, which is the aspect of the inner dimension of the roots of the souls, as above. Therefore then they all return to their root through the <span class="key-term">kol shofar</span>, as above.</p>

<p>The meaning of <span class="key-term">apotaiki</span>: <span class="aramaic">apo t'hai ka'i</span> — "upon this it shall stand." For the money is the aspect of <span class="key-term">regel</span> [foot], which is the aspect of standing. As our Sages, <em>zichronam livrachah</em>, said <span class="source">(Pesachim 119a)</span>: <span class="scripture">"And all the wealth [<span class="key-term">y'kum</span>] that was at their feet"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 11:6)</span> — this is a person's money, which stands him upon his feet. And this is <span class="key-term">apo t'hai ka'i</span>: "from here shall be your money," which is the aspect of his feet, as above.</p>

<div class="translator-summary">
<h3>Summary of G'viyas Chov Min HaLikuchos V'Apotiki 1</h3>
<p>Continuous essay (no osiyos, 9,666 Hebrew chars). Core framework: Why the creditor's shi'bud applies to karka'os even after sale to a purchaser, but not to mitaltelim.</p>
<p>Karka'os = ikkar shoresh ha'ashirus = nisrashin b'nafsho b'yoser → sale is never absolute (p'nimiyus shorshan remains with seller). Proof: in Yovel era, land cannot be sold litz'misus ("v'ha'aretz lo simachair litz'misus ki Li ha'aretz," Vayikra 25:23). Therefore ba'al chov toreif from karka'os even miyad halokai'ach (lien persists through sale).</p>
<p>Mitaltelim = b'chinas peiros, not so rooted → sale is absolute → teichef yotz'in meirshus lirshus → shi'bud nifka. Even apotaiki m'forash doesn't help (apotaiki = only shi'bud, not m'chirah g'murah).</p>
<p>Hekdeish chameitz v'shichrur mafki'in midei shi'bud: Only k'dushas haguf (not Hekdeish damim) releases, because korban removes p'nimiyus shoresh hanefesh. Explained through s'michah: "v'samach es yado alav" (Vayikra 1:4) — the yad holds p'nimiyus kol han'fashos v'haruchos ("b'yad'cha afkid ruchi," T'hilim 31:6; "asher b'yado nefesh kol chai," Iyov 12:10 — as per LM I:54). Through s'michah, p'nimiyus nefesh ascends with korban → fully exits his r'shus → shi'bud released.</p>
<p>Shichrur: avadim hukshu l'karka'os. Slave = domeh l'ishah (chayav b'mitzvos sh'ha'ishah chayeves) → b'chinas ishah/karka/olam. Freed only through get shichrur (= get k'risus) because rooted in nefesh → removes p'nimiyus → releases shi'bud. Chameitz/isurei hana'ah: motzi'o l'gamrei meirshuso → mafkia.</p>
<p>Kol: Karka'os and eved yeish lahem kol = b'chinas ruach = p'nimiyus shoresh hanefesh (kol = samuch l'dibur always = ruach v'nefesh). Mitaltelim = anfei hashoresh → ain lahem kol → ain shi'bud. In Yovel: through kol shofar → fields return (shofar = reveals p'nimiyus shorshei han'fashos).</p>
<p>Apotiki = "apo t'hai ka'i" (here it shall stand). Mamon = b'chinas regel/amidah: "v'es kol hay'kum asher b'raglaihem = mamono shel adam shema'amido al raglav" (Pesachim 119a; D'varim 11:6).</p>
<p class="translator-note">Based on teachings explained in the preceding Hilchos G'viyas Chov Min HaY'somim · G'viyas Chov Min HaLikuchos V'Apotiki 1 complete.</p>
